header is kept. The upstream version it was taken from is not recorded
in this repository. This modified driver is not BlackHole, does not use
the BlackHole name for its device, and is not made or endorsed by
Existential Audio Inc.

Modifications (Acoustic Orbit, 2026):

1. Build identity (build.sh defines, driver version 4, 20 Oct 2026):
   driver name AcousticOrbitTap, device and manufacturer name
   "Acoustic Orbit", the hidden second device "Acoustic Orbit Mirror",
   16 channels, bundle identifier com.acousticorbit.tap (bundle
   AcousticOrbitTap.driver, executable AcousticOrbitTap), no icon;
   device UIDs AcousticOrbitTap_UID and AcousticOrbitTap_2_UID, model
   UID AcousticOrbitTap_ModelUID. Linked against Accelerate. Versions 1
   to 3 were built as driver name SpeakerLCRTap, device and manufacturer
   "Speaker LCR", bundle identifier com.snehasis.speakerlcr.tap, UIDs
   SpeakerLCRTap_UID and SpeakerLCRTap_2_UID.
2. A published latency for lip-sync: kAudioDevicePropertyLatency can be
   set by the app (at most 192000 frames) and is applied through a
   device configuration change (ChangeAction_SetLatency), so video
   players delay the picture to match the sound. The driver itself adds
   no delay.
3. A custom property 'lclt' that carries the same latency figure as a
   string, listed in kAudioObjectPropertyCustomPropertyInfoList.
4. Each of the driver's two device objects keeps its own latency value
   (they used to share one).
5. A 16-channel build reports the Atmos 9.1.6 layout as its preferred
   channel layout: sixteen channel descriptions in the 9.1.6 order
   (since driver version 3, 20 Oct 2026; version 2 reported the single
   Atmos 9.1.6 tag, 18 Oct 2026); other channel counts keep BlackHole's
   channel descriptions.
